  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DtZ- Stepping Up the Fight Against Sexual Exploitation of Children (SUFASEC): EU component</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The SUFASEC programme is designed to combat SEC by working towards the following long-term impact: &amp;ldquo;Children in all of their diversity are better protected from sexual exploitation.&amp;rdquo;&amp;nbsp; The long-term impact will be reached through three interlinking objectives that address different dimensions (social norms, assets/environments, and laws/policies/systems).&amp;nbsp;
The different stakeholder groups involved in the SUFASEC programme include: Children and youth in all their diversity, Caregivers and Communities, CSOs and CBOs, Local and national governments, Private Secto, International donors, Intergovernmental bodies, INGOs, Multilateral entities, Dutch Stakeholders,&amp;nbsp;Media &amp;amp; Journalists</narrative>
  </description>
